WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:05.509
Aladdin left the palace with his head hanging down.

2
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.391
Feeling hopeless, he walked through the city gate.

3
00:00:07.411 --> 00:00:09.212
The land was wide open outside the city walls.

4
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:10.192
Soon Aladdin came to a swift river and sat down.

5
00:00:32.956 --> 00:00:35.598
"Oh, Princess, how will I ever find you?"

6
00:00:36.258 --> 00:00:37.138
Aladdin wondered.

7
00:00:38.299 --> 00:00:39.600
"Will I ever see you again?"

8
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.301
He stared at the rippling water.

9
00:00:42.321 --> 00:00:45.623
"I should just throw myself into this river."

10
00:00:46.904 --> 00:00:49.305
He put his face in his hands and wept.

11
00:00:50.206 --> 00:00:54.908
When he finally wiped the tears away, he noticed something on one of his fingers.

12
00:00:54.928 --> 00:00:57.550
"Magrib's ring!"

13
00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:58.931
cried Aladdin.

14
00:00:58.951 --> 00:01:01.152
"The little genie!"

15
00:01:01.888 --> 00:01:05.009
He rubbed the ring until a cloud of bright smoke appeared.

16
00:01:05.029 --> 00:01:09.230
"The genie of the ring has come!"

17
00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.651
squeaked the little man with bells on his cap.

18
00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:14.272
"What's the problem?"

19
00:01:14.292 --> 00:01:20.233
"Oh, genie," said Aladdin, "bring back my palace and my wife!"

20
00:01:20.253 --> 00:01:23.994
"Your wish is my command, master!"

21
00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:27.175
said the little genie as he raised his arms.

22
00:01:28.356 --> 00:01:29.476
Then he stopped.

23
00:01:30.232 --> 00:01:32.874
"Did you ask me to bring back your palace and your wife?"

24
00:01:32.894 --> 00:01:36.676
"Yes, I did," Aladdin answered.

25
00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:40.579
"Well, I've got bad news," said the genie of the ring.

26
00:01:40.599 --> 00:01:42.220
"I can't do it.

27
00:01:43.661 --> 00:01:47.144
The genie of the lamp's magic took your palace and your wife.

28
00:01:47.844 --> 00:01:48.825
Where is the lamp?"

29
00:01:50.726 --> 00:01:53.708
"I don't know," said Aladdin, feeling sad again.

30
00:01:53.728 --> 00:01:59.432
"Sorry, I cannot undo another genie's magic," replied the genie.

31
00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.301
"Those are the rules."

32
00:02:03.661 --> 00:02:05.962
"Wait, can you take me to the princess?"

33
00:02:05.982 --> 00:02:07.822
"Of course!"

34
00:02:08.442 --> 00:02:09.182
said the genie.

35
00:02:09.202 --> 00:02:10.863
"Let's go!"

36
00:02:14.484 --> 00:02:18.045
When Aladdin found himself outside his palace, it was night.

37
00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.886
His home was dark and quiet.

38
00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:24.727
"I'll wait until morning," Aladdin told himself.

39
00:02:25.907 --> 00:02:29.308
He lay down under Princess Badra's window and fell asleep.

40
00:02:31.712 --> 00:02:35.433
The next morning, the princess was sitting in her room with her attendants.

41
00:02:36.713 --> 00:02:39.874
From time to time, she sighed and wiped away a tear.

42
00:02:39.894 --> 00:02:44.315
"This is such a strange place," she cried.

43
00:02:44.335 --> 00:02:47.136
"And where is my Aladdin?"

44
00:02:47.156 --> 00:02:55.479
"Maybe some fresh air will bring color to your cheeks," said one attendant as she opened a window.

45
00:02:55.499 --> 00:03:00.580
"Nothing will help me feel better," said the princess sadly.

46
00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:04.589
"Princess!" shouted the woman at the window.

47
00:03:04.609 --> 00:03:08.871
"Look! I see Aladdin asleep under the window!"

48
00:03:10.532 --> 00:03:12.653
Princess Badra ran over to look.

49
00:03:12.673 --> 00:03:15.254
"Aladdin!" she called out.

50
00:03:15.274 --> 00:03:17.315
"My dear husband!"

51
00:03:18.595 --> 00:03:23.638
Aladdin's eyes quickly opened, and he looked up to see his wife's beautiful face.

52
00:03:25.598 --> 00:03:26.779
"Run and open the door!"

53
00:03:27.459 --> 00:03:28.940
said the princess to a servant.

54
00:03:30.196 --> 00:03:34.838
Within moments, Aladdin was racing up the steps toward the princess's room.

55
00:03:36.058 --> 00:03:40.100
But instead of embracing her, he ran straight into his bedroom.

56
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.361
"My lamp!"

57
00:03:42.921 --> 00:03:45.042
he cried as he rushed back to the princess.

58
00:03:45.062 --> 00:03:46.303
"Where is my lamp?"

59
00:03:46.323 --> 00:03:49.784
"It is gone," said the princess.

60
00:03:49.804 --> 00:03:53.566
"I traded it to an old man for a new lamp.

61
00:03:54.146 --> 00:03:56.607
Then all of a sudden, I ended up in Egypt."

62
00:03:58.688 --> 00:04:00.305
"Egypt!" said Aladdin.

63
00:04:00.325 --> 00:04:02.246
"Magrib must have done this!"

64
00:04:03.626 --> 00:04:05.808
Aladdin described the magician to his wife.

65
00:04:05.828 --> 00:04:07.428
"Was he the old man?"

66
00:04:07.448 --> 00:04:11.071
"Yes, husband," the princess replied.

67
00:04:11.091 --> 00:04:13.152
"I don't like him.

68
00:04:13.672 --> 00:04:14.733
He smells funny."

69
00:04:14.753 --> 00:04:18.074
"Where does Magrib keep the lamp?"

70
00:04:18.715 --> 00:04:19.495
Aladdin asked.

71
00:04:20.756 --> 00:04:23.417
"He carries it in his coat," said the princess.

72
00:04:24.558 --> 00:04:27.680
"He shows it to me and smiles strangely when he visits."

73
00:04:29.044 --> 00:04:29.824
"He visits you?"

74
00:04:30.325 --> 00:04:31.005
said Aladdin.

75
00:04:31.025 --> 00:04:34.906
"Yes," answered the princess.

76
00:04:34.926 --> 00:04:38.687
"He comes every day and asks me to marry him.

77
00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:43.049
He told me you were dead, but I didn't believe him."

78
00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:45.770
Aladdin thought a moment.

79
00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.851
Then he told Princess Badra what she had to do.
